From 5fbe306c8f84c7176a7fcb5a0b4ba065b3c509ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: noname <noname@example.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:53:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 0031] Let the mouse turn the game instead of pointing at it

A game that looks with the mouse reads raw movement, not a position: a position
stops at the edge of the screen, and so does the turn. Until now the stream
window forwarded where the pointer was, which is enough for a menu and useless
for aiming.

While the window is fullscreen the pointer is now locked to it
(zwp_pointer_constraints_v1), the movement is read from
zwp_relative_pointer_v1 and sent as opennow_streamer_submit_mouse_relative. The
windowed form keeps absolute positions, because that is the form used to reach
the interface, and the lock is not guaranteed to activate: while it has not, the
position keeps being forwarded, so nothing regresses on a compositor that does
not grant it.

The fraction of a surface unit is carried over between events instead of being
rounded away, so a slow turn is not lost.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [STM32MP25 performance work]
---
